    "created_at": "2021-01-27T00:49:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-27T00:51:33Z",
    "body": "> Remove the `<T>` from promise types entirely. It seems this better matches implementations.\r\n\r\nHi, sorry for jumping into a rather technical discussion about things over my head, but I'd wager promises are predominantly output-to-JS, not input-from-ES, so I'm not convinced the value of `<T>` should hang in the balance over problems in the latter category.\r\n\r\nIn my view `Promise<T>` has normative value in declaring API outputs that user agents MUST implement even if WebIDL tools can't enforce anything about them. I'm very thankful that it exists.🙏 ❤️ See https://github.com/heycam/webidl/issues/951#issuecomment-767915892.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
