    "updated_at": "2021-01-27T06:11:29Z",
    "body": "I'm pretty sure that service workers rely on the type being enforced when an arbitrary promise is passed in (e.g., for `respondWith()`. And once we make ByteString map to a byte sequence and vice versa I could see it being useful for return values as well. I don't see why promises would be different from synchronous callbacks/functions.",
